Id: ssh009w
Severity: WARN
Category: ssh
Check: check_ssh
Fix: Set MaxAuthTries 4.
References: sshd_config(5); CIS Ubuntu Linux 24.04 LTS Benchmark v2.0.0, 5.1.16 (Ensure sshd MaxAuthTries is configured)
Controls: CIS 4.1, 5.4; NIST AC-17, IA-2; ISO 8.5, 8.20; CE Secure configuration, User access control

MaxAuthTries is above 4 (the default is 6), which gives a
password-guessing client more attempts per connection before it is
dropped. CIS asks for 4 or fewer, and 4 passes here; Lynis wants 3, and
Tigris follows the benchmark. Once half the limit is reached the
remaining failures are logged (sshd_config(5)).
